💡 **SUGGESTION: stale cross-reference — this comment still cites the old 5-minute cap**

The clause below was written against the pre-PR cap, but this same PR raises the file cap to 10 minutes (line 6). As committed, the two comments contradict each other: the header says the 10-min backstop is needed *because* the 5-minute cap starves the assertion waits, while this line says 180s boot "leaves the file's 5-minute per-test cap room" — a cap that no longer exists in this file.

Suggested wording (matches the budget arithmetic in the PR description):

```dart
      // job_card_heredoc_pty_test.dart (#604); 180s boot + the waits
      // below (≈ 286s worst case) sit well inside the file's 10-minute
      // per-test cap.
```

Comment-only, no behavioral impact — fine to fix in a follow-up or with the next touch of this file.

